APPENDIX A - THE JUSTCODE RECIPROCITY ADDENDUM (applies in addition to Apache-2.0)
================================================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Aghosh ("JustCode") and the Q Grid community (Qub3RAM.team)

In addition to every permission granted by the Apache License 2.0 above, the
following reciprocal condition governs COMMERCIAL DEPLOYMENT of the Work or a
Derivative Work. The short version, in plain language:

    "You can use it. You can rebuild it. You can even sell it. But if you sell
     it, you owe me a copy of your new version - and I won't make it public."

    - To big companies, yours truly, Aghosh, aka JustCode.

1. PERMISSIONS.
   You may use, study, copy, rebuild, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
   sublicense and sell the Work and Derivative Works, in source or object
   form, worldwide, royalty-free - exactly as Apache-2.0 already allows.

2. RECIPROCITY ON SALE.
   If you SELL the Work or a Derivative Work - whether standalone, bundled
   with other software, or as a substantial component of a paid product or
   paid service - then you must provide the original author (Aghosh,
   "JustCode") with a complete, buildable copy of your new version, including
   source code for all modifications, free of charge:
     (a) within thirty (30) days of your first commercial sale or first day
         of paid operation, and
     (b) again within thirty (30) days of each subsequent major version you
         sell.
   Delivery to the contact published in the project README (or any successor
   channel the project names) satisfies this clause.

3. CONFIDENTIALITY OF THE DELIVERED COPY.
   The copy delivered under clause 2 is used solely to verify license
   compliance and to maintain interoperability with the upstream project.
   The original author will NOT publish, redistribute, showcase, or
   competitively exploit that copy. Your improvements remain yours to keep
   closed; this clause asks for a copy, never for disclosure.

4. SCOPE - WHAT IS UNAFFECTED.
   Personal use, internal business use, academic use, contributions offered
   back to the Q Grid project, and commercial *services that do not sell the
   Work itself* (e.g. operating a charging network with Q Grid) are NOT
   subject to clause 2. Only the act of selling the Work or a Derivative
   Work triggers reciprocity.

5. PRECEDENCE.
   This addendum imposes additional conditions on top of Apache-2.0; it does
   not subtract any permission Apache-2.0 grants. If any provision of this
   addendum is held unenforceable, the remainder of the license continues in
   full force, and the provision shall be reformed to the minimum extent
   necessary to preserve the reciprocity intent.

6. INTENT.
   Q Grid is community-funded and community-governed. This addendum exists so
   that the project's founder and its community of contributors and
   shareholders stay first in line to see what the work they funded evolves
   into - while keeping the core free for everyone else.
